[[{"text": "NSW HSC 4 Unit Mathematics Examination 1978", "x0": 0.253475935828877, "y0": 0.12396694214876033, "x1": 0.7497326203208556, "y1": 0.1347107438016529}, {"text": "1. (i) Use Buclid\u2019s algorithm to find the highest common factor of 1247 and 2537", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.16033057851239668, "x1": 0.8577540106951872, "y1": 0.1743801652892562}, {"text": "and show that it can be expressed in the form", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.17851239669421487, "x1": 0.5401069518716578, "y1": 0.1925619834710744}, {"text": "1247p + 2537q", "x0": 0.44278074866310163, "y0": 0.21239669421487603, "x1": 0.5614973262032086, "y1": 0.2256198347107438}, {"text": "in an infinite number of ways (with p,q as integers).", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.24462809917355371, "x1": 0.5903743315508021, "y1": 0.25867768595041324}, {"text": "(ii) Ifa,", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.271900826446281, "x1": 0.22566844919786097, "y1": 0.2859504132231405}, {"text": "are given integers prove that the equation", "x0": 0.24919786096256685, "y0": 0.271900826446281, "x1": 0.6064171122994653, "y1": 0.2859504132231405}, {"text": "ar", "x0": 0.453475935828877, "y0": 0.3090909090909091, "x1": 0.4727272727272727, "y1": 0.315702479338843}, {"text": "has integers solutions for (x,y) if and only if d divides \u00a2 where d is the highest", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.33884297520661155, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.3528925619834711}, {"text": "common factor of a, b.", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.35619834710743803, "x1": 0.3336898395721925, "y1": 0.3685950413223141}, {"text": "Tf (xo, yo) is one such solution prove that any othe le in", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.38264462809917354, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.3975206611570248}, {"text": "solution must be expre:", "x0": 0.5935828877005348, "y0": 0.3834710743801653, "x1": 0.788235294117647, "y1": 0.3975206611570248}, {"text": "the form", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.40165289256198344, "x1": 0.21818181818181817, "y1": 0.412396694214876}, {"text": "na", "x0": 0.5914438502673797, "y0": 0.41818181818181815, "x1": 0.611764705882353, "y1": 0.42479338842975206}, {"text": "y=yo-\u2014", "x0": 0.5262032085561498, "y0": 0.428099173553719, "x1": 0.6128342245989304, "y1": 0.43471074380165287}, {"text": "ot", "x0": 0.4374331550802139, "y0": 0.4297520661157025, "x1": 0.44385026737967914, "y1": 0.4371900826446281}, {"text": "where n is an integer.", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.4553719008264463, "x1": 0.32941176470588235, "y1": 0.46942148760330576}, {"text": "2. (i) If a, 8,7 are the three roots of", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.49173553719008267, "x1": 0.4588235294117647, "y1": 0.5057851239669422}, {"text": "x 4+pr+q=0", "x0": 0.43529411764705883, "y0": 0.5223140495867769, "x1": 0.5679144385026738, "y1": 0.5396694214876033}, {"text": "(p,q being constants) find the cubic equation whose roots are a?, 3?, 77.", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.556198347107438, "x1": 0.7614973262032085, "y1": 0.5727272727272728}, {"text": "(ii) When a polynomial P(x) is divided by \u20142 and by \u00ab\u20143 the respective remainders", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.5859504132231405, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.6}, {"text": "are 4 and 9; determine what the remainder must be when it is divided by (x \u20142)(x\u2014", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.6033057851239669, "x1": 0.8556149732620321, "y1": 0.6181818181818182}, {"text": "3).", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.6223140495867768, "x1": 0.16684491978609625, "y1": 0.6363636363636364}, {"text": "3. (i) For a particle of mass m moving in a straight line under the action of a variable", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.6487603305785123, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.6768595041322314}, {"text": "force prove that, over a given interval, the work done by the force is equal to the", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.6760330578512397, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.6900826446280992}, {"text": "increase in kinetic energy.", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.6942148760330579, "x1": 0.36149732620320857, "y1": 0.7082644628099174}, {"text": "(ii) A mass of 20 kilograms hangs from the end of a rope and is hauled up vertically", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.7214876033057851, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.7355371900826446}, {"text": "from rest by winding up the rope. The pulling force in the rope starts at 250 newtons", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.7396694214876033, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.7537190082644628}, {"text": "and decreases uniformly by 10 newtons for every metre wound up. Find the velocity", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.7578512396694215, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.771900826446281}, {"text": "of the mass after 10 metres have been wound up. (Take the acceleration due to", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.775206611570248, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.7900826446280992}, {"text": "gravity as 9.8 m/s? and neglect the weight of the rope.)", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.7917355371900826, "x1": 0.6213903743315508, "y1": 0.8082644628099174}, {"text": "4. (i) A,B,C are three points on horizontal ground forming a triangle with a right-", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.8305785123966942, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.8446280991735537}, {"text": "angle at the lengths of the sides BC, CA are a,b respectively. Vertical borings", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.8487603305785124, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.8628099173553719}, {"text": "are made at A, B,C and coal is struck at points P,Q, R at respective depths p, q,7-", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.8578512396694215, "x1": 0.8556149732620321, "y1": 0.8859504132231405}, {"text": "If 4 is the inclination of the plane PQR to the horizontal prove that", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.8752066115702479, "x1": 0.7283422459893049, "y1": 0.903305785123967}, {"text": "(q=r) +", "x0": 0.4577540106951872, "y0": 0.9165289256198347, "x1": 0.5433155080213904, "y1": 0.9380165289256198}, {"text": "=", "x0": 0.43422459893048126, "y0": 0.9314049586776859, "x1": 0.4470588235294118, "y1": 0.9355371900826446}], [{"text": "u", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.09008264462809917, "x1": 0.16149732620320856, "y1": 0.09834710743801653}, {"text": "(ii) The two spheres", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.12396694214876033, "x1": 0.3165775401069519, "y1": 0.13801652892561983}, {"text": "cut in a circle 3. Find the equation of the sphere that contains this circle 3 and also", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.19834710743801653, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.21239669421487603}, {"text": "passes through the origin.", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.21652892561983472, "x1": 0.36470588235294116, "y1": 0.23057851239669422}, {"text": "5. Define the modulus |z| of a complex number z.", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.2528925619834711, "x1": 0.5700534759358289, "y1": 0.26776859504132233}, {"text": "Given two complex numbers 21,22 prove that:", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.2809917355371901, "x1": 0.5379679144385027, "y1": 0.2950413223140496}, {"text": "(i) =", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.3082644628099174, "x1": 0.23850267379679144, "y1": 0.32231404958677684}, {"text": "(ii) the triangle represented (on the Argand diagram) by the complex numbers 0, 1, 21", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.33636363636363636, "x1": 0.8545454545454545, "y1": 0.3504132231404959}, {"text": "milar to the triangle represented by 0, 22, 2122;", "x0": 0.17967914438502675, "y0": 0.35454545454545455, "x1": 0.574331550802139, "y1": 0.3685950413223141}, {"text": "(iii) \u2014 2? + [21 + = + and interpret this as a theorem on a", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.3793388429752066, "x1": 0.8577540106951872, "y1": 0.3958677685950413}, {"text": "triangle giving the length of a median in terms of the lengths of the sides.", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.4, "x1": 0.7764705882352941, "y1": 0.4140495867768595}, {"text": "6. (i) Prove that the series", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.43636363636363634, "x1": 0.3732620320855615, "y1": 0.4512396694214876}, {"text": "2\u00b073 n", "x0": 0.4267379679144385, "y0": 0.4925619834710744, "x1": 0.560427807486631, "y1": 0.503305785123967}, {"text": "is divergent by first proving that the sum of the first 2\u201d terms exceeds n/2", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.5231404958677686, "x1": 0.7839572192513369, "y1": 0.5380165289256198}, {"text": "Also prove that the sum of the first thousand term is less than 10.", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.5512396694214876, "x1": 0.7122994652406417, "y1": 0.5652892561983471}, {"text": "(ii) Investigate for convergence the series whose term is", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.5793388429752067, "x1": 0.6524064171122995, "y1": 0.5933884297520661}, {"text": "(a) 3255 (where x is positive);", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.6049586776859505, "x1": 0.4042780748663102, "y1": 0.6247933884297521}, {"text": "(b)", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.6388429752066116, "x1": 0.17005347593582887, "y1": 0.6528925619834711}, {"text": "7. Evaluate (giving numerical answers to three significant figures):", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.6760330578512397, "x1": 0.7122994652406417, "y1": 0.6900826446280992}, {"text": "@ fy", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.7016528925619835, "x1": 0.1925133689839572, "y1": 0.7223140495867768}, {"text": "(ii) de;", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.7396694214876033, "x1": 0.3048128342245989, "y1": 0.7537190082644628}, {"text": "(iii) [2\u00b0 de:", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.7669421487603306, "x1": 0.25989304812834224, "y1": 0.7876033057851239}, {"text": "(iv) f2 sin\u201c! x de.", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.7983471074380165, "x1": 0.30267379679144385, "y1": 0.8214876033057851}, {"text": "8. In the cart", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.8421487603305785, "x1": 0.253475935828877, "y1": 0.8528925619834711}, {"text": "an plane sketch the curve", "x0": 0.28449197860962566, "y0": 0.8421487603305785, "x1": 0.5005347593582887, "y1": 0.856198347107438}, {"text": "\u00a5", "x0": 0.4449197860962567, "y0": 0.8925619834710744, "x1": 0.453475935828877, "y1": 0.9024793388429752}, {"text": "e+e*", "x0": 0.4834224598930481, "y0": 0.9, "x1": 0.5550802139037433, "y1": 0.9099173553719008}, {"text": "and prove that the lines y = +1 are asymptotes.", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.9314049586776859, "x1": 0.5572192513368984, "y1": 0.9454545454545454}], [{"text": "15", "x0": 0.8427807486631016, "y0": 0.09008264462809917, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.09834710743801653}, {"text": "Also, if k is a positive constant, find the area in the positive quadrant enclosed by", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.12396694214876033, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.13801652892561983}, {"text": "the above curve and the three lines", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.14214876033057852, "x1": 0.4459893048128342, "y1": 0.15289256198347106}, {"text": "and prove that this area is always less than log, 2, however large k may be.", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.21487603305785125, "x1": 0.788235294117647, "y1": 0.22892561983471074}, {"text": "9. In the cartesian plane the point P, whose co-ordinates are (r,y), is transformed", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.25041322314049586, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.2644628099173554}, {"text": "to the point P', whose co-ordinates are by the affine transformation Ar", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.26859504132231404, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.28264462809917357}, {"text": "where A is a matrix and", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.28677685950413223, "x1": 0.35614973262032085, "y1": 0.2975206611570248}, {"text": "Determine the matrix A in the following cases:", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.35619834710743803, "x1": 0.5422459893048128, "y1": 0.3702479338842975}, {"text": "(i) is obtained from P by reflection in the line", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.3834710743801653, "x1": 0.5668449197860963, "y1": 0.3975206611570248}, {"text": "(ii) P\u2019 is the mid-point of the segment OP (O being the origin);", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.4644628099173554, "x1": 0.6941176470588235, "y1": 0.4793388429752066}, {"text": "(iii) P\u2019 is the foot of the perpendicular from P on the line", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.49173553719008267, "x1": 0.6427807486631016, "y1": 0.5066115702479339}, {"text": "ax =0 (where a,b are constants).", "x0": 0.3336898395721925, "y0": 0.528099173553719, "x1": 0.6684491978609626, "y1": 0.5421487603305785}, {"text": "10. (i) In the cartesian plane the (\u00ab,y) co-ordinate frame is rotated about the origin", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.5818181818181818, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.596694214876033}, {"text": "anti-clockwise through an angle @ to give a new frame with co-ordinates denoted", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.6008264462809917, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.6148760330578512}, {"text": "by Derive equations expressing the transformation between the two sets of", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.6190082644628099, "x1": 0.8588235294117647, "y1": 0.6330578512396694}, {"text": "co-ordinates (x,y) and (x\u2019,y\u2019).", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.6363636363636364, "x1": 0.4053475935828877, "y1": 0.6512396694214876}, {"text": "(ii) Prove that (in cartesian co-ordinates)", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.6636363636363637, "x1": 0.4983957219251337, "y1": 0.6785123966942149}, {"text": "22\" + =6", "x0": 0.4203208556149733, "y0": 0.6942148760330579, "x1": 0.5871657754010695, "y1": 0.7181818181818181}, {"text": "represents an hyperbola. Illustrate its shape and position by a clear diagram show-", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.7371900826446282, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.7512396694214876}, {"text": "ing, in particular, its asymptotes and principal axes. Also, write down the equations", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.7462809917355372, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.7743801652892562}, {"text": "off", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.7735537190082644, "x1": 0.1625668449197861, "y1": 0.7842975206